<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Remediation plan: {{ alias }}</title>
<style>{{ base_css }}</style>
<style>
  /* Components specific to the plan, built on the shared tokens. */
  .phase-intro { color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 40rem; }
  .card .detail { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .card ol, .card ul { margin: 0.4rem 0 0.4rem 1.3rem; padding: 0; }
  .card li { margin: 0.45rem 0; }
  .alert {
    border: 1px solid var(--bad);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    background: var(--bad-tint);
  }
  .alert strong { color: var(--bad); }
  .checkpoint {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--warn);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
  }
  .checkpoint .query { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  pre.comms {
    background: var(--surface-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 0.95em;
  }
  @media print { .checkpoint, pre.comms { background: #ffffff; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>

<div class="brandbar"><span class="mark">iA</span> IAMAI <span class="sub">&middot; remediation plan</span></div>
<h1>Remediation plan</h1>
<p class="meta">Tenant: {{ alias }}. Generated {{ generated_at }}.
Rollout starts {{ start_date }}.
Based on the assessment generated {{ based_on }}.
License tier assumed: {{ license_tier }}.</p>

<h2>How to read this plan</h2>
<p>This plan is a series of steps grouped into phases, with a measured
checkpoint at the end of each phase. A checkpoint is a statement that is
checked against fresh data, not a date on the wall. When a checkpoint is not
met, the phases that depend on it wait until it is: the dates move, the order
never does, and nothing here expires. To check a checkpoint, run the
collection and assessment again and compare the result to its statement.</p>
<p>Work one step at a time, top to bottom, and tick the boxes as you go. The
actions are the heart of each step. The folded sections underneath hold the
reference detail: how the step is verified, how to roll it back, and what to
watch for. Select a folded section to open it; open the ones you want on
paper before printing.</p>

<h2>The rollout at a glance</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Phase</th><th>Days</th><th>Dates</th><th>Checkpoint to pass</th></tr>
  {% for phase in phases %}
  <tr>
    <td>{{ phase.number }}. {{ phase.name }}</td>
    <td>{{ phase.days }}</td>
    <td>{{ phase.dates }}</td>
    <td>{{ phase.gateId }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>

<h2>The checkpoints</h2>
{% for gate in gates %}
<div class="checkpoint">
  <strong>{{ gate.id }}.</strong> {{ gate.statement }}
  <p class="query">How to check: {{ gate.query }}.</p>
  <p class="query">If not met: {{ gate.extensionRule }}</p>
</div>
{% endfor %}

{% for phase in phases %}
<h2>Phase {{ phase.number }}: {{ phase.name }}</h2>
<p class="eyebrow">{{ phase.days }} &middot; {{ phase.dates }}</p>
<p class="phase-intro">{{ phase.purpose }}
{% if gates_by_id.get(phase.gateId) %}Checkpoint to pass before the next phase: {{ gates_by_id[phase.gateId].statement }}{% endif %}</p>
{% for step in steps_by_phase.get(phase.number, []) %}
<section class="card">
  <header>
    <span class="eyebrow">Step {{ positions[step.id] }} of {{ total_steps }}</span>
    <span class="risk {{ step.riskClass }}"><span class="dot"></span>{{ risk_labels[step.riskClass] }}</span>
  </header>
  <div class="title-row"><span class="tick"></span><h3>{{ step.title }}</h3></div>
  <p class="detail">Accounts this affects: {{ step.affected.count }}{% if step.affected.samples %}
  (for example {% for sample in step.affected.samples %}{{ sample }}{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}){% endif %}</p>

  {% set failing = step.preconditions | selectattr("result", "equalto", "fail") | list %}
  {% if failing %}
  <div class="alert"><strong>Fix before this step:</strong>
    <ul>
    {% for pre in failing %}<li>{{ pre.statement }} <span class="detail">Checked by: {{ pre.query }}.</span></li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <h4>Actions</h4>
  <ol class="actions">
  {% for action in step.actions %}<li>{{ action }}</li>{% endfor %}
  </ol>

  {% for biglist in step.lists %}
  <details>
    <summary>{{ biglist.title }}: {{ biglist.summary }}</summary>
    <ul>
    {% for item in biglist['items'] %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </details>
  {% endfor %}

  <details>
    <summary>Before you start: {{ step.preconditions | length }} check{{ 's' if step.preconditions | length != 1 }}</summary>
    <ul>
    {% for pre in step.preconditions %}
      <li><span class="pre-{{ pre.result }}">[{{ precondition_labels[pre.result] }}]</span>
      {{ pre.statement }} <span class="detail">Checked by: {{ pre.query }}.</span></li>
    {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Reference: how this step is verified, rolled back, and what to watch for</summary>
    <h4>How this step is verified</h4>
    <p class="detail">{{ step.verification.query }}. Expected: {{ step.verification.expected }}
    Current status: {{ step.verification.status }}.</p>
    <h4>If something goes wrong</h4>
    <ol>
    {% for item in step.rollback %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ol>
    <h4>Watch for</h4>
    <ul>
    {% for item in step.watchFor %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </details>

  <p class="detail">Step {{ step.id }}{% if step.controlId %} for control {{ step.controlId }}{% endif %}</p>
</section>
{% else %}
<p class="detail">No steps in this phase for this tenant.</p>
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

<h2>Watch list</h2>
{% if watch_list %}
{% set accounts = watch_list | selectattr("kind", "equalto", "account") | list %}
{% set applications = watch_list | selectattr("kind", "equalto", "application") | list %}
<p>Accounts and applications to keep an eye on for the whole rollout:
{{ watch_list | length }} item{{ 's' if watch_list | length != 1 }}
({{ accounts | length }} account{{ 's' if accounts | length != 1 }},
{{ applications | length }} application{{ 's' if applications | length != 1 }}).</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Item</th><th>Kind</th><th>Why</th></tr>
  {% for item in watch_list[:8] %}
  <tr><td>{{ item.item }}</td><td>{{ item.kind }}</td><td>{{ item.reason }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% if watch_list | length > 8 %}
<details>
  <summary>Show the remaining {{ watch_list | length - 8 }} of {{ watch_list | length }} watch list items</summary>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Item</th><th>Kind</th><th>Why</th></tr>
    {% for item in watch_list[8:] %}
    <tr><td>{{ item.item }}</td><td>{{ item.kind }}</td><td>{{ item.reason }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
</details>
{% endif %}
{% else %}
<p>Nothing needs special monitoring beyond the step cards.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if best_effort_note %}
<h2>What this plan can reach</h2>
<p>{{ best_effort_note }}</p>
{% endif %}

{% if not_included %}
<h2>Not included in this plan</h2>
<p>These protections are graded below the standard but the plan leaves them
out, with the reason stated honestly.</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Protection</th><th>Why it is not included</th></tr>
  {% for item in not_included[:8] %}
  <tr><td>{{ item.title }} ({{ item.controlId }})</td><td>{{ item.reason }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% if not_included | length > 8 %}
<details>
  <summary>Show the remaining {{ not_included | length - 8 }} of {{ not_included | length }} protections</summary>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Protection</th><th>Why it is not included</th></tr>
    {% for item in not_included[8:] %}
    <tr><td>{{ item.title }} ({{ item.controlId }})</td><td>{{ item.reason }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
</details>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

<h2>What this plan cannot see</h2>
<p>An honest list of blind spots. Nothing here was guessed around.</p>
<ul>
{% for item in unknowns[:8] %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% if unknowns | length > 8 %}
<details>
  <summary>Show the remaining {{ unknowns | length - 8 }} of {{ unknowns | length }} items</summary>
  <ul>
  {% for item in unknowns[8:] %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
  </ul>
</details>
{% endif %}

<h2>Communication templates</h2>
<p>Ready to send messages, populated with this plan's checkpoints and real
dates. This tool never sends anything itself.</p>
{% for name, text in comms.items() %}
<h4>{{ comms_titles.get(name, name) }}</h4>
<pre class="comms">{{ text }}</pre>
{% endfor %}

<footer>
<p>{{ scope_note }}</p>
<p>To keep a copy, print this page to PDF from the browser. Open any folded
sections you want on paper first.</p>
<p class="attribution">Generated by IAMAI, a read only, open source Microsoft Entra
identity posture tool. Every step here is carried out by a person; the tool changes nothing.</p>
</footer>

</main>
</body>
</html>
